>term classItem = (λitem.cases(regex.ClassItem){character=λc.printCodePoint c, range=λr.strings.concat [printCodePoint (regex.CharacterRange[`from`] r), "-", printCodePoint (regex.CharacterRange[to] r)]} item)@{description="Render one character-class member (a single character or an inclusive range). Emacs bracket expressions do NOT support backslash escaping (probe-verified: \\- and \\] inside [...] are two literal characters, not an escape); the metacharacters ] ^ - are instead disambiguated positionally by characterClass (] first, - last, ^ never first), so a plain character or range here never needs an escape."}
